dear editors,

i would like to send you *the small blue*, a short story, for your spring issue.

ada comes home to clear out her mother's house and finds the garden still running on its timer. over one summer she learns the beds, the shed and the apple tree, and on the last warm morning of october a small blue butterfly lands on the lavender by the gate, months after the others have gone.

the story is the last chapter of a longer piece i am writing about one garden, told from the gate. it has not been published anywhere else.

thank you for reading.

#v(1em)

with best wishes,

